From 61acc084b84b89546dcc30d5e3c9f1cb610bae33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:10:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/53] embedded: persist command history through the host app

The web build has no local database, so command metadata (exit code, times, cwd, git branch,
shell/host) went nowhere and was lost on reload. Embedded builds now report started/finished
commands to window.warpPanelRecordCommand and load persisted history from
window.warpPanelCommandHistory at startup, mirroring desktop's SQLite commands table. The
finished-command history update no longer requires a persistence sender, which also fixes
exit codes in in-memory history on the web.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
